  "scope_notes": [
    "The full Python gate preceded test-only preprocessor guards for TSan allocation interceptors; production source stayed byte-identical. Final native and sanitizer gates used the guarded sources.",
    "Release benchmark cache had ANNDATA_BUILD_EXAMPLES=OFF, hence 18 native groups; Debug and shared Release include the import-only example.",
    "TSan build intentionally targets four focused executables and omits custom allocation overrides; native and ASan retain allocation observations.",
    "Normal Python huge fixture retained a 512 MiB address-space limit. ASan omitted only that incompatible limit, with address and undefined sanitizers active. LeakSanitizer was disabled for runner restrictions.",
    "Shard replacement is atomic per active file through temp/rename; prior shard changes can remain after a later failure. Data-dependent oversized old encoded payloads can fail during processing.",
    "Scratch caps cover owned transfer workspace, not caller buffers, third-party codec internal allocations, or whole-process RSS.",
    "HDF5 and unsharded irregular destinations retain a bounded logical-run fallback. Large owned regions can delay adaptive candidate sampling.",
    "Performance timings are single matched observations with instrumentation and warm caches; no general device or workload speedup is claimed.",
    "Initial Release CTest found no tests in the benchmark-only cache; tests were enabled, built and the full 18-group gate then passed. The no-tests observation is recorded here and in the tool history; no failed gate is counted as passed.",
